      <div class="article__main">
        <div class="article__body prose">
          <blockquote>
<ul>
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> GTA 6 has <strong>two playable leads</strong>, <strong>Jason Duval</strong> and <strong>Lucia Caminos</strong>. The game is <strong>single-player</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>You can switch between them</strong>, in free roam and in missions, per GameSpot and VGC. You can split up or stay together.</li>
<li><strong>Character and story details are hidden</strong> in spoiler boxes below. Only open them if you want to know.</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Words used on this page.</strong> <em>Playable lead</em> is a character you control. <em>Free roam</em> is when you play outside a mission. <em>Spoiler box</em> is a box you open if you want that detail.</p>
<h2 id="how-the-pair-plays" tabindex="-1">How the pair plays</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Single-player:</strong> PlayStation’s FAQ says “Grand Theft Auto VI is a single-player experience.”</li>
<li><strong>Two leads:</strong> you can swap between Jason and Lucia in free roam and during missions. In one example from previews, one drives while the other shoots. (GameSpot, VGC)</li>
<li><strong>Story time:</strong> Rob Nelson’s own playthrough, focused on the main story and story-based extras, took about <strong>80 hours</strong> (GameSpot). This is one person’s estimate, not a promise.</li>
<li><strong>Romance is optional</strong>, per previews (PC Gamer, Game Informer via Mapheist). They stay partners either way.</li>
<li><strong>Voice cast:</strong> not officially announced by Rockstar. Do not treat press mentions as final.</li>
</ul>
<p>![Jason and Lucia switch screen](TODO: image:jason-lucia-step-1 — menu screen, only after launch: the character switch prompt; before launch use Designer’s own art of two silhouettes)
<em>Caption: Menu screen. How the switch between Jason and Lucia looks, once we can show it.</em></p>
<h2 id="the-setup-in-one-line" tabindex="-1">The setup, in one line</h2>
<details class="spoiler"><summary class="spoiler__summary"><span class="spoiler__label">What the trailers revealed about their story (premise only, no ending)</span><span class="spoiler__hint" aria-hidden="true">tap to reveal</span></summary><div class="spoiler__body" data-pagefind-ignore>
<p>Rockstar’s own setup: Jason and Lucia know the odds are against them. When an “easy score” goes wrong, they end up in the middle of a criminal conspiracy across the state of Leonida. They have to trust each other more than ever. Source: Rockstar and Take-Two press release.</p>
</div></details>
<h2 id="jason-duval" tabindex="-1">Jason Duval</h2>
<details class="spoiler"><summary class="spoiler__summary"><span class="spoiler__label">Jason: who he is, from Rockstar&#39;s character page (early background)</span><span class="spoiler__hint" aria-hidden="true">tap to reveal</span></summary><div class="spoiler__body" data-pagefind-ignore>
<p>Jason grew up around grifters and crooks. He served in the Army after a troubled youth. He ended up in the Keys, working for local drug runners, and wants an easier life. Source: <a href="https://www.rockstargames.com/VI/lucia" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">https://www.rockstargames.com/VI/lucia</a></p>
</div></details>
<h2 id="lucia-caminos" tabindex="-1">Lucia Caminos</h2>
<details class="spoiler"><summary class="spoiler__summary"><span class="spoiler__label">Lucia: who she is, from Rockstar&#39;s character page (early background)</span><span class="spoiler__hint" aria-hidden="true">tap to reveal</span></summary><div class="spoiler__body" data-pagefind-ignore>
<p>Lucia’s father taught her to fight when she was little. Fighting for her family got her sent to the Leonida Penitentiary. She is out now, and wants only smart moves from here. She wants the good life her mom has dreamed of since their days in Liberty City. Source: <a href="https://www.rockstargames.com/VI/lucia" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">https://www.rockstargames.com/VI/lucia</a></p>
</div></details>
<p>![two character cards with names only](TODO: image:jason-lucia-step-2 — diagram, Designer’s original art: two blank character cards labelled Jason Duval and Lucia Caminos, no Rockstar art without credit)
<em>Caption: Diagram. The two playable leads.</em></p>
<h2 id="the-supporting-cast" tabindex="-1">The supporting cast</h2>
<details class="spoiler"><summary class="spoiler__summary"><span class="spoiler__label">Names and one-line roles from Rockstar&#39;s site (no story)</span><span class="spoiler__hint" aria-hidden="true">tap to reveal</span></summary><div class="spoiler__body" data-pagefind-ignore>
<ul>
<li><strong>Cal Hampton:</strong> Jason’s friend, a conspiracy-minded homebody.</li>
<li><strong>Brian Heder:</strong> a veteran smuggler in the Keys who lets Jason stay in one of his properties.</li>
<li><strong>Raul Bautista:</strong> a bank robber. (PC Gamer spells it “Batista”. Wikipedia and previews say “Bautista”. We use Bautista and will verify on Rockstar’s page.)</li>
<li><strong>Boobie Ike:</strong> a Vice City local legend with business in real estate, a club and a record label.</li>
<li><strong>Dre’Quan Priest:</strong> a music hustler tied to that label, Only Raw Records.</li>
<li><strong>Real Dimez:</strong> a rap duo, Bae-Luxe and Roxy, signed to the same label.</li>
</ul>
</div></details>
<h2 id="how-the-game-tracks-your-behaviour" tabindex="-1">How the game tracks your behaviour</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Criminal Profile:</strong> previews describe a reputation system that tracks professional versus needless violence. It is not cleared like wanted stars. (GameSpot, Wikipedia)</li>
<li><strong>Wanted stars return</strong> (six-star system). People react, and call police, if you carry guns in public. (GameSpot)</li>
<li><strong>Not announced:</strong> exact number of missions and endings.</li>
</ul>
<p>![icons for switching, wanted stars, criminal profile](TODO: image:jason-lucia-step-3 — diagram, our own art: three icons for switching leads, six wanted stars, criminal profile)
<em>Caption: Diagram. Three systems tied to Jason and Lucia.</em></p>
<h2 id="faq" tabindex="-1">FAQ</h2>
<h3 id="who-are-the-main-characters-in-gta-6" tabindex="-1">Who are the main characters in GTA 6?</h3>
<p>Jason Duval and Lucia Caminos. You play both.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-switch-between-them" tabindex="-1">Can I switch between them?</h3>
<p>Yes, per previews, in free roam and in missions.</p>
<h3 id="is-gta-6-single-player" tabindex="-1">Is GTA 6 single-player?</h3>
<p>Yes. PlayStation’s FAQ says it is a single-player experience.</p>
<h3 id="does-this-page-have-spoilers" tabindex="-1">Does this page have spoilers?</h3>
<p>No. Everything about the characters and story is inside boxes you open on purpose.</p>
